WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.801
When you look at your voting record

00:00:01.801 --> 00:00:02.435
and the issues

00:00:02.435 --> 00:00:03.703
that are important to you

00:00:03.703 --> 00:00:05.605
as spelled out on your website,

00:00:05.605 --> 00:00:07.240
most of them are traditional

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:08.208
democratic issues.

00:00:08.208 --> 00:00:10.377
Capital, Capital, D,

00:00:10.377 --> 00:00:12.812
expanding health care, access,

00:00:12.812 --> 00:00:15.782
abortion rights, LGBTQ rights,

00:00:16.816 --> 00:00:19.352
path for Dreamers, and on and on.

00:00:19.352 --> 00:00:21.421
Environmentalism, green energy.

00:00:21.654 --> 00:00:23.823
That sounds like a Democrat to me.

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:24.924
No.

00:00:25.392 --> 00:00:27.727
Well, I know this is really hard

00:00:27.727 --> 00:00:29.996
for a lot of folks, especially in D.C..

00:00:30.797 --> 00:00:35.001
But what's important to me is to not be

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:39.572
to not be tethered by the Partizanship

00:00:40.407 --> 00:00:42.776
that dominates politics today.

00:00:42.942 --> 00:00:45.311
And I think Americans are tired of it.

00:00:45.311 --> 00:00:47.280
I think Arizonans are tired of it.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:48.681
What I'm interested in

00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:49.215
is working

00:00:49.215 --> 00:00:50.216
on all those issues

00:00:50.216 --> 00:00:51.151
that you just mentioned

00:00:51.151 --> 00:00:52.652
that I care deeply about

00:00:52.652 --> 00:00:53.653
and that I believe

00:00:53.653 --> 00:00:55.822
my constituents care deeply about.

00:00:55.822 --> 00:00:56.723
But I want to work on them

00:00:56.723 --> 00:00:58.491
in a way that is productive,

00:00:58.491 --> 00:01:00.827
that is free, from the trappings

00:01:00.827 --> 00:01:02.962
of the pull of the political system.

00:01:03.363 --> 00:01:04.998
You know, the national political parties

00:01:04.998 --> 00:01:07.233
have pulled our politics farther

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:09.803
to the edges than I've ever seen.

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:11.371
I want to

00:01:11.371 --> 00:01:12.939
remove some of that

00:01:12.939 --> 00:01:15.141
kind of that poison from our politics.

00:01:15.508 --> 00:01:16.976
I want to get back to actually

00:01:16.976 --> 00:01:18.645
just working on the issues,

00:01:18.645 --> 00:01:20.280
working together to try and solve

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:21.381
these challenges.

00:01:21.381 --> 00:01:22.415
And one of the big complaints

00:01:22.415 --> 00:01:23.416
I hear from conservatives,

00:01:23.416 --> 00:01:25.151
from Republicans, is Democrats

00:01:25.151 --> 00:01:25.985
just don't take border

00:01:25.985 --> 00:01:27.320
security seriously.

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:28.988
They just don't

00:01:29.956 --> 00:01:31.724
Do you agree with that sentiment?

00:01:31.724 --> 00:01:34.627
And do you think there is an actual

00:01:34.627 --> 00:01:35.595
path forward there?

00:01:35.595 --> 00:01:36.963
Democrats are still going

00:01:36.963 --> 00:01:38.164
to have the majority in the next Senate

00:01:38.164 --> 00:01:39.899
you can still get this

00:01:39.899 --> 00:01:42.135
on the floor of the Senate if you want.

00:01:42.135 --> 00:01:43.703
Well, as a native Arizonan

00:01:43.703 --> 00:01:44.337
who was born

00:01:44.337 --> 00:01:46.239
and raised near the southern border,

00:01:46.239 --> 00:01:48.308
I can tell you unequivocally

00:01:48.308 --> 00:01:49.976
that the federal government has failed

00:01:49.976 --> 00:01:50.643
its duty

00:01:50.643 --> 00:01:52.178
in the last 40 years,

00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:53.113
not just Democrats,

00:01:53.113 --> 00:01:54.547
not it's just everyone.

00:01:54.547 --> 00:01:56.583
The federal government has failed here.

00:01:56.583 --> 00:01:57.417
And places

00:01:57.417 --> 00:01:58.151
like Arizona

00:01:58.151 --> 00:02:01.321
on the front lines of this crisis

00:02:01.654 --> 00:02:02.555
have been paying the price

00:02:02.555 --> 00:02:04.324
every single day since then.

00:02:04.324 --> 00:02:06.860
So for us, this isn't just a talking

00:02:06.860 --> 00:02:09.062
point of team versus TV.

00:02:09.362 --> 00:02:11.731
This is our life every day.

00:02:11.865 --> 00:02:14.100
The reality is, is that when folks say,

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:15.001
you know,

00:02:15.001 --> 00:02:17.470
we've got to just provide a legal path

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:18.938
to citizenship, for Dreamers,

00:02:18.938 --> 00:02:21.107
which I support wholeheartedly.

00:02:21.541 --> 00:02:24.244
These kids are Americans in all but name.

00:02:25.145 --> 00:02:26.579
So when folks say, we've got to do that,

00:02:26.579 --> 00:02:27.547
I agree.

00:02:27.547 --> 00:02:28.281
And when folks say

00:02:28.281 --> 00:02:29.315
we've got to secure the border,

00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:30.750
of course I agree.

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:30.984
You know,

00:02:30.984 --> 00:02:32.051
my state is suffering

00:02:32.051 --> 00:02:34.687
from the failure to do so for 40 years.

00:02:34.687 --> 00:02:37.757
So this is a perfect example of why

00:02:37.757 --> 00:02:40.560
I'm so frustrated with Partizanship

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:42.695
that has gripped our nation.

00:02:42.695 --> 00:02:45.098
And the parties are pulling folks away.

00:02:45.098 --> 00:02:46.332
It's not either or.

00:02:46.332 --> 00:02:47.400
It's and

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:48.101
both of

00:02:48.101 --> 00:02:51.271
those concerns are real and valid.

00:02:51.704 --> 00:02:52.972
And we as a government

00:02:52.972 --> 00:02:54.440
have a duty to solve

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:56.242
both of those concerns.

00:02:56.242 --> 00:02:58.778
You're up for reelection in 20, 24.

00:02:59.579 --> 00:03:00.480
This move means,

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:01.447
I suppose, that you're not

00:03:01.447 --> 00:03:02.749
going to be running

00:03:02.749 --> 00:03:04.050
in the Democratic primary

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:05.652
for the Senate seat.

00:03:05.718 --> 00:03:06.953
Well, again,

00:03:06.953 --> 00:03:07.187
I know

00:03:07.187 --> 00:03:07.687
this will probably

00:03:07.687 --> 00:03:08.821
be disappointing to folks,

00:03:08.821 --> 00:03:10.890
but I'm actually not even thinking

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:12.258
about electoral politics

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:14.093
or talking about that at all right now.

00:03:14.093 --> 00:03:14.561
But doesn't

00:03:14.561 --> 00:03:15.695
this increase the likelihood

00:03:15.695 --> 00:03:16.896
that your run for reelection

00:03:16.896 --> 00:03:17.463
will be tougher

00:03:17.463 --> 00:03:18.498
because you will not only have

00:03:18.498 --> 00:03:19.766
a Republican opponent,

00:03:19.766 --> 00:03:22.168
you may even have a Democratic opponent?

00:03:22.168 --> 00:03:23.169
You know, I

00:03:23.236 --> 00:03:24.604
don't make decisions based on what

00:03:24.604 --> 00:03:26.673
the easy road or the tough road is.

00:03:26.673 --> 00:03:28.441
I have always tried to make decisions

00:03:28.441 --> 00:03:30.176
based on what I think is right.

00:03:30.176 --> 00:03:32.345
And for me, it's very important

00:03:32.912 --> 00:03:34.714
that we have a discussion

00:03:34.714 --> 00:03:36.115
at home in Arizona

00:03:36.115 --> 00:03:38.351
and here in the nation's capital

00:03:38.952 --> 00:03:41.354
about reducing the partizanship

00:03:41.354 --> 00:03:44.424
and just focus on solving the challenges

00:03:44.424 --> 00:03:45.792
that we face in America.

00:03:45.792 --> 00:03:47.961
The challenges we face are great.

00:03:47.961 --> 00:03:49.229
They're significant.

00:03:49.229 --> 00:03:51.631
We cannot solve them

00:03:51.631 --> 00:03:53.766
by using partizan attacks.

00:03:53.766 --> 00:03:55.301
We cannot solve them

00:03:55.301 --> 00:03:57.170
through a partizan lens.

00:03:57.170 --> 00:03:58.404
And I want to be a part

00:03:58.404 --> 00:04:00.406
of having that discussion

00:04:01.274 --> 00:04:01.808
and showing

00:04:01.808 --> 00:04:03.576
that there is a different way.

00:04:03.576 --> 00:04:05.011
Would you ever run for president?

00:04:05.011 --> 00:04:07.080
No, never. I don't want to be president.

00:04:07.547 --> 00:04:09.048
There are two independents

00:04:09.048 --> 00:04:09.782
who already caucus

00:04:09.782 --> 00:04:10.683
with the Democrats, Bernie

00:04:10.683 --> 00:04:11.751
Sanders of Vermont and Angus

00:04:11.751 --> 00:04:12.585
King of Maine.

00:04:12.585 --> 00:04:13.920
Lisa Murkowski,

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:14.721
who's a Republican

00:04:14.721 --> 00:04:16.089
but ran

00:04:16.155 --> 00:04:17.890
in a previous election as an independent

00:04:19.826 --> 00:04:21.160
is also,

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:21.995
you know, somebody who

00:04:21.995 --> 00:04:24.597
whose independence is now noted.

00:04:24.597 --> 00:04:24.897
Are the

00:04:24.897 --> 00:04:27.267
are those three models at all

00:04:27.267 --> 00:04:28.134
for what you're doing?

00:04:28.134 --> 00:04:30.370
Are there other independents

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:32.672
Teddy Roosevelt in the Bull Moose Party?

00:04:32.672 --> 00:04:33.940
Is there anyone you look to

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:35.208
as a as a guide,

00:04:35.208 --> 00:04:36.943
as a mentor, as a role model

00:04:36.943 --> 00:04:39.279
when it comes to what you're doing?

00:04:39.279 --> 00:04:39.812
You Jake,

00:04:39.812 --> 00:04:40.647
it probably won't surprise you

00:04:40.647 --> 00:04:41.114
when I tell you

00:04:41.114 --> 00:04:43.416
I'm not trying to be like anyone else.

00:04:43.416 --> 00:04:45.618
What I'm trying to do is be true

00:04:45.618 --> 00:04:47.920
to my values and the values of my state.

00:04:48.655 --> 00:04:49.555
So you know,

00:04:49.555 --> 00:04:49.856
I think

00:04:49.856 --> 00:04:52.191
everyone should make their own decisions

00:04:52.191 --> 00:04:54.327
about where they fit

00:04:54.327 --> 00:04:56.963
or where they don't fit.

00:04:57.096 --> 00:04:57.730
I'm going to keep doing

00:04:57.730 --> 00:04:58.698
exactly what I do,

00:04:58.698 --> 00:05:01.301
which is just stay focused on the work,

00:05:01.567 --> 00:05:04.404
you know, and ignore all the noise

00:05:06.706 --> 00:05:07.473
Here with me now

00:05:07.473 --> 00:05:08.041
is somebody

00:05:08.041 --> 00:05:09.208
who knows a thing or two

00:05:09.208 --> 00:05:10.476
about going his own way.

00:05:10.476 --> 00:05:11.411
Independent Senator

00:05:11.411 --> 00:05:13.313
Bernie Sanders of Vermont.

00:05:13.313 --> 00:05:16.683
Senator, first, you are an independent.

00:05:16.683 --> 00:05:17.950
She is now the third

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:19.786
official independent of the U.S.

00:05:19.786 --> 00:05:21.054
Senate, joining

00:05:21.054 --> 00:05:22.855
you and Angus King of Maine.

00:05:22.855 --> 00:05:23.990
What do you think of her decision

00:05:23.990 --> 00:05:24.757
and also what

00:05:24.757 --> 00:05:25.892
you just heard in her interview?

00:05:25.892 --> 00:05:26.826
With Jake

00:05:28.461 --> 00:05:30.396
I don't want to spend a whole lot of time

00:05:30.396 --> 00:05:31.564
on Senator Cinema.

00:05:31.564 --> 00:05:33.900
She has her reasons, Don.

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:35.935
I happen to suspect that

00:05:35.935 --> 00:05:38.071
it's probably a lot to do

00:05:38.071 --> 00:05:40.039
with politics back in Arizona.

00:05:40.039 --> 00:05:40.807
I think

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:41.774
the Democrats

00:05:41.774 --> 00:05:43.443
there are not all that enthusiastic

00:05:43.443 --> 00:05:45.611
about somebody who helped sabotage

00:05:45.611 --> 00:05:47.380
some of the most important legislation

00:05:47.380 --> 00:05:49.716
that protects the interests

00:05:49.716 --> 00:05:52.352
of working families and voting rights

00:05:52.352 --> 00:05:53.653
and so forth.

00:05:53.653 --> 00:05:56.122
So I think it really has to do with her

00:05:56.122 --> 00:05:58.291
political aspirations

00:05:58.291 --> 00:05:59.625
for the future in Arizona.

00:05:59.625 --> 00:06:00.793
But for us,

00:06:00.793 --> 00:06:02.995
I think nothing much has changed

00:06:02.995 --> 00:06:03.730
in terms

00:06:03.730 --> 00:06:05.898
of the functioning of the US Senate.

00:06:05.898 --> 00:06:08.601
The good news is that we now have

00:06:08.601 --> 00:06:09.535
51 votes,

00:06:09.535 --> 00:06:10.837
we'll have majority on committees.

00:06:10.837 --> 00:06:12.271
That means that we can go forward

00:06:12.271 --> 00:06:14.440
and start protecting the interests

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:15.408
of the working families

00:06:15.408 --> 00:06:16.442
to deal with the reality

00:06:16.442 --> 00:06:17.944
that we are increasing things.

00:06:17.944 --> 00:06:20.012
Living in an oligarchy

00:06:20.012 --> 00:06:21.714
where the billionaire class

00:06:21.714 --> 00:06:23.549
and large corporations

00:06:23.549 --> 00:06:24.016
control

00:06:24.016 --> 00:06:25.952
almost every aspect of our country.

00:06:25.952 --> 00:06:27.620
So I would hope very much

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:29.122
that with this new majority,

00:06:29.122 --> 00:06:30.690
Democrats will sit down and start

00:06:30.690 --> 00:06:31.858
fighting for the needs

00:06:31.858 --> 00:06:32.925
of ordinary Americans.

00:06:32.925 --> 00:06:33.960
So I want to talk about

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:35.461
some of those issues in a second.

00:06:35.461 --> 00:06:36.429
But first,

00:06:36.429 --> 00:06:37.964
you were a very important

00:06:37.964 --> 00:06:38.965
figure on the campaign

00:06:38.965 --> 00:06:40.199
trail for progressives

00:06:40.199 --> 00:06:41.167
ahead of the midterms,

00:06:41.167 --> 00:06:42.902
as you normally are.

00:06:42.902 --> 00:06:44.270
I'm sure you're going to be campaigning

00:06:44.270 --> 00:06:45.638
for candidates in 20, 20

00:06:45.638 --> 00:06:47.306
for the outgoing

00:06:47.306 --> 00:06:49.509
Arizona Democratic Party official.

00:06:49.876 --> 00:06:50.676
One of them says that

00:06:50.676 --> 00:06:51.210
he expects

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:52.912
Democrats will run their own candidate

00:06:52.912 --> 00:06:54.347
against her.

00:06:54.347 --> 00:06:55.381
Is that a good idea?

00:06:55.381 --> 00:06:57.583
Would you support a Democratic opponent

00:06:57.583 --> 00:06:59.352
against Senator Cinema? I don't.

00:07:00.653 --> 00:07:01.554
I support

00:07:01.554 --> 00:07:02.588
progressive candidates

00:07:02.588 --> 00:07:03.623
all over this country,

00:07:03.623 --> 00:07:04.991
people who have the guts to take

00:07:04.991 --> 00:07:06.926
on powerful special interests.

00:07:06.926 --> 00:07:07.493
I don't know what's

00:07:07.493 --> 00:07:08.728
going to be happening in Arizona.

00:07:08.728 --> 00:07:10.196
We'll see who they nominate.

00:07:10.196 --> 00:07:10.797
But certainly

00:07:10.797 --> 00:07:11.764
that's something I will take a hard

00:07:11.764 --> 00:07:12.131
look at.

00:07:12.131 --> 00:07:13.399
Does she have the guts to take

00:07:13.399 --> 00:07:15.635
on powerful special interests?

00:07:15.635 --> 00:07:16.636
No, she doesn't.

00:07:16.636 --> 00:07:18.871
She has a corporate Democrat

00:07:18.871 --> 00:07:20.206
who has, in fact,

00:07:20.206 --> 00:07:21.441
along with Senator Manchin,

00:07:21.441 --> 00:07:22.642
sabotaged

00:07:22.642 --> 00:07:25.211
enormously important legislation.

00:07:25.211 --> 00:07:27.780
I want to talk about a major deadline

00:07:27.780 --> 00:07:29.115
to fund the government.

00:07:29.115 --> 00:07:30.850
That is Friday.

00:07:30.850 --> 00:07:32.118
There's still no deal.

00:07:32.118 --> 00:07:32.985
Would you support

00:07:32.985 --> 00:07:33.753
another short term

00:07:33.753 --> 00:07:35.521
extension instead of a larger

00:07:35.521 --> 00:07:36.756
bill to fund the government

00:07:36.756 --> 00:07:38.157
and how worried are you about

00:07:38.157 --> 00:07:38.624
the government?

00:07:38.624 --> 00:07:40.259
Well, short term

00:07:40.593 --> 00:07:42.662
short term extensions are just

00:07:42.662 --> 00:07:43.930
a temporary solution

00:07:43.930 --> 00:07:46.432
to the ongoing crisis we face.

00:07:46.432 --> 00:07:48.601
Are clearly what I worry about

00:07:48.968 --> 00:07:50.470
is Republican efforts

00:07:51.504 --> 00:07:53.372
to hold hostage next year.

00:07:53.372 --> 00:07:56.008
If we don't get an omnibus bill passed

00:07:56.008 --> 00:07:59.779
to hold or hold hostage

00:08:00.613 --> 00:08:02.281
the government

00:08:02.281 --> 00:08:03.816
in order to cut Social Security,

00:08:03.816 --> 00:08:04.784
Medicare and Medicaid,

00:08:04.784 --> 00:08:05.051
and that,

00:08:05.051 --> 00:08:06.786
I will vigorously oppose

00:08:06.786 --> 00:08:08.354
you and a lot of seniors out there.

00:08:08.354 --> 00:08:09.355
We're not making it on

00:08:09.355 --> 00:08:10.756
Social Security today.

00:08:10.756 --> 00:08:12.358
A lot of working people of

00:08:12.358 --> 00:08:14.060
who are approaching retirement,

00:08:14.060 --> 00:08:15.228
who have nothing in the bank.

00:08:15.228 --> 00:08:16.863
I don't want to see Social Security

00:08:16.863 --> 00:08:17.797
or Medicare cut.

00:08:17.797 --> 00:08:19.098
I will oppose that vigorously.

00:08:19.098 --> 00:08:20.466
You know, while I have you,

00:08:20.466 --> 00:08:22.602
you've been in Congress a long time.

00:08:22.602 --> 00:08:24.437
The House before the Senate, there

00:08:24.437 --> 00:08:25.705
certainly have been some notable

00:08:25.705 --> 00:08:27.907
bipartisan pieces of legislation

00:08:27.907 --> 00:08:28.474
that have passed

00:08:28.474 --> 00:08:29.542
and been signed into law,

00:08:29.542 --> 00:08:32.245
but arguably funding the government is

00:08:32.912 --> 00:08:33.346
up there,

00:08:33.346 --> 00:08:35.414
maybe even the top responsibility

00:08:35.414 --> 00:08:36.182
of you

00:08:36.182 --> 00:08:37.583
and your fellow members of Congress.

00:08:37.583 --> 00:08:38.918
Why does this keep happening?

00:08:41.320 --> 00:08:43.523
Well, I think it's happening right now

00:08:43.523 --> 00:08:44.624
because Republicans

00:08:44.624 --> 00:08:47.226
see it as an opportunity

00:08:47.226 --> 00:08:49.529
to hold us hostage

00:08:49.896 --> 00:08:51.497
and get demands

00:08:51.497 --> 00:08:53.799
that under normal circumstances

00:08:53.799 --> 00:08:54.300
they would not

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:55.535
look they have

00:08:55.601 --> 00:08:57.603
not been shy about making it clear

00:08:58.170 --> 00:08:59.672
they want to cut Social Security,

00:08:59.672 --> 00:09:00.606
they want to cut Medicare,

00:09:00.606 --> 00:09:02.408
they want to cut Medicaid.

00:09:02.408 --> 00:09:03.543
And what they're saying is, hey,

00:09:03.543 --> 00:09:04.911
we are prepared

00:09:04.911 --> 00:09:05.678
to allow

00:09:05.678 --> 00:09:06.812
the United States government

00:09:06.812 --> 00:09:08.881
to default on our payments,

00:09:08.881 --> 00:09:10.249
bring the entire world

00:09:10.249 --> 00:09:12.451
perhaps into an economic crisis center

00:09:12.652 --> 00:09:14.754
unless you give us what you want.

00:09:14.754 --> 00:09:16.522
What you're saying about the differences

00:09:16.522 --> 00:09:16.956
right now.

00:09:16.956 --> 00:09:18.024
But over the past

00:09:18.024 --> 00:09:19.058
many years, Democrats

00:09:19.058 --> 00:09:20.660
and Republicans in charge

00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:21.060
funding

00:09:21.060 --> 00:09:22.795
the government has just not happened.

00:09:22.795 --> 00:09:24.063
And we've been at this crisis

00:09:24.063 --> 00:09:25.398
point at the end of.

00:09:25.398 --> 00:09:26.732
At the end of the year, so,

00:09:26.732 --> 00:09:27.567
so many times.

00:09:27.567 --> 00:09:28.768
But I want to move on to

00:09:28.768 --> 00:09:29.769
a couple more issues

00:09:29.769 --> 00:09:31.103
that I know that you care about.

00:09:31.103 --> 00:09:32.104
One is

00:09:32.438 --> 00:09:36.042
the record breaking $858 billion defense

00:09:36.042 --> 00:09:37.443
funding bill.

00:09:37.443 --> 00:09:39.145
The House passed that this week.

00:09:39.145 --> 00:09:41.781
The Senate is going to vote on it.

00:09:42.081 --> 00:09:44.517
You voted against the NDAA,

00:09:44.517 --> 00:09:46.319
the defense bill last time around.

00:09:46.319 --> 00:09:47.253
Will you do so again?

00:09:49.155 --> 00:09:50.556
Yes, I think I will.

00:09:50.556 --> 00:09:53.259
Look, we have

00:09:53.392 --> 00:09:55.127
we have 85 million Americans

00:09:55.127 --> 00:09:56.963
who have no health insurance.

00:09:56.963 --> 00:09:59.832
We have 600,000 people who are homeless.

00:10:00.800 --> 00:10:02.902
We have a dysfunctional health

00:10:02.902 --> 00:10:03.936
care system,

00:10:03.936 --> 00:10:05.671
dysfunctional childcare system.

00:10:05.671 --> 00:10:08.441
Working parents are paying $15,000

00:10:08.441 --> 00:10:11.844
a year on average for child care.

00:10:11.844 --> 00:10:14.013
We have got to start protecting the needs

00:10:14.280 --> 00:10:15.815
of working families.

00:10:15.815 --> 00:10:17.283
The Pentagon is the one

00:10:17.283 --> 00:10:18.751
major agency of government

00:10:18.751 --> 00:10:19.652
which has never been

00:10:19.652 --> 00:10:21.153
independently audited.

00:10:21.153 --> 00:10:24.156
There is massive waste and fraud

00:10:25.257 --> 00:10:27.760
and cost overruns within that agency.

00:10:28.260 --> 00:10:30.663
So I think we can have the strong defense

00:10:30.663 --> 00:10:31.564
that we need

00:10:31.564 --> 00:10:33.666
without spending the huge amount of money

00:10:33.666 --> 00:10:35.167
that we're currently spending

00:10:35.167 --> 00:10:36.035
on the military.

